  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/D364">Theorem <span data-tag="D364">5.1.5.6</span>.</a>presheaf!universal property of $\calP (S)$ Let $S$ be a small simplicial set, and let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category which admits small colimits. Composition with the Yoneda embedding $j: S \rightarrow \calP (S)$ induces an equivalence of $\infty $-categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \LFun ( \calP (S), \calC ) \rightarrow \Fun (S,\calC ). \]
</div>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Corollary <a href="/tag/74C1" data-tag="74C1">4.3.2.16</a> with Lemma <a href="/tag/C391" data-tag="C391">5.1.5.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>